# Backend Access Runbook

This runbook blocks direct public access to the Cloud Run `run.app` URL while keeping the Google Load Balancer URL available.

## Current Values

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Cloud Run service | `interview-backend` |
| Cloud Run region | `asia-south1` |
| Direct Cloud Run URL | `https://interview-backend-10476774711.asia-south1.run.app` |
| Load Balancer API URL | `https://services.answerflow-ai.com` |

## Before You Restrict Access

Confirm the load balancer endpoint is healthy:

```powershell
curl.exe --ssl-no-revoke -i https://services.answerflow-ai.com/api/test
```

Expected result:

```text
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
```

Do not restrict Cloud Run ingress until this path works.

## Block Direct Cloud Run Public Access

Run:

```powershell
gcloud run services update interview-backend `
  --region asia-south1 `
  --ingress internal-and-cloud-load-balancing
```

This allows traffic from the Google Load Balancer and blocks direct public requests to:

```text
https://interview-backend-10476774711.asia-south1.run.app
```

## Validate After The Change

Direct Cloud Run access should now fail:

```powershell
curl.exe --ssl-no-revoke -i https://interview-backend-10476774711.asia-south1.run.app/api/test
```

The load balancer path should still work:

```powershell
curl.exe --ssl-no-revoke -i https://services.answerflow-ai.com/api/test
```

## Rollback

If the load balancer path fails after restricting ingress, temporarily restore direct public Cloud Run access:

```powershell
gcloud run services update interview-backend `
  --region asia-south1 `
  --ingress all
```

Then fix the load balancer, DNS, certificate, or serverless NEG configuration before restricting ingress again.

## Important Note

For this setup, keep unauthenticated invocation enabled if the public load balancer should reach the backend without identity-aware proxy or custom service-to-service auth.

The ingress setting controls which network paths can reach Cloud Run. The IAM invoker setting controls who can invoke it. To block only the raw `run.app` URL, use ingress restriction first.
